he  big challenge we overcrowding as people  are uncomfortable because there's too  many in small areas we're gonna be able  to reduce that really hard to watch no  other mother having to be interviewed  through a fence you know and the emotion  is right there on the surface two or  three questions and tears I keep  thinking about these people that are so  desperate to get away from the  conditions where they're living but they  want to come to a place where they know  they're not even welcome when they get  here it's still better than where what  they've come in much rather come here  and take their chances heartbreaking it  is you can see more of Nora's exclusive  reporting tonight on the CBS Evening  News she'll take us to the banks of the  Rio Grande River where the journey into  the u.s. immigration system began for  the families that she met
 

